<title>USA: Federal judge halts Ill. tollway expansion-report.</title>
<headline>Federal judge halts Ill. tollway expansion-report.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A federal court judge in Chicago on Thursday halted plans for a $700 million, bond-financed expansion of the tollway system in northeastern Illinois, according to local newspaper reports.</p>
<p>U.S. District Judge Suzanne Conlon ruled that Illinois did not properly study alternatives to the tollroad and did not adequately assess its impact on the environment, the Chicago Sun-Times reported.</p>
<p>The ruling came in a lawsuit filed by environmental groups in August. That lawsuit claimed the environmental impact statement for the project was flawed.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
